{
  "id": "pika-text-to-video",
  "name": "Pika Text to Video",
  "section": "video",
  "pack": "video-h3",
  "status": "ready",
  "workflow": "workflow.api.json",
  "summary": "Text to video with Pika H3 Flex (fl2va adapters, empty reference bin) and its own sound. Optional 2×/4× upscale.",
  "higgsfield_feature": "Create Video",
  "source": {
    "template": "video_pika_h3_flex_t2v.json",
    "comfyui": "0.43.0",
    "notes": "ComfyUI's Pika H3 Flex t2v template, flattened from its 'Image to Video (Pika H3 Flex)' subgraph with both keyframe slots empty. Local additions: H3SLAAttentionROCM (0.85 sparsity, bypassable) and an optional RelayVSR x2/x4 pass (the same DIT + Flash VAE as the RelayVSR Upscale app) that is bypassed when set to None. Default resolution 0.98 MP, lcm sampler and 6-step sigma ladder unchanged. Local controls: sampling mode (Pika 6-step ladder or custom BasicScheduler), steps, sampler, LoRA picker (Pika Flex default; turbo LoRAs switch to their own step count and sampler), DiT and video VAE pickers, SLA sparsity/block/dense options."
  },
  "inputs": [
    {
      "id": "prompt",
      "type": "textarea",
      "label": "Prompt",
      "required": true,
      "default": "integrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] Stylized 3D animation, Pixar-inspired cartoon rendering with a C4D and Octane look, warm subsurface scattering through ears and fingertips and exaggerated squash-and-stretch acting; a three-head-tall cook with a round face, a tall white toque that flops to one side and a flour-dusted apron stands at a stainless counter in a small warm kitchen, rolling dumplings by hand. The counter is dusted white, a bamboo steamer steams on the right, and a shallow pot of broth sits at the burner behind him with visible heat shimmer. The camera holds a static shot at counter height for the first second while he sets one finished dumpling down on a tray in the foreground, presses the seam with two fingers, then turns away to reach for a rolling pin on the shelf behind him, the toque tipping as he turns. At about one and a half seconds the dumpling on the tray presses itself upward, its pleated top gathering like a brow, and two stubby legs of dough push out of its base. It walks to the tray edge in three quick shuffling steps, the tray ringing slightly under each step, and jumps off toward the pot. At about two and a half seconds the cook whips around and lunges, both arms out, and misses clean over the top of it as the dumpling arcs into the broth with a plop. He freezes half-bent over the pot, arms still out. At about three and a half seconds the surface breaks and the dumpling floats back up, cooked, glossy and steaming, bobbing once against the side of the pot. The last second holds completely still on the cook's face as he straightens up slowly, flour on his cheek, the toque now fully flopped over one eye, one eyebrow rising while his mouth stays flat; a single bubble pops on the broth behind him.\n\noverall_soundscape: Warm small-kitchen ambience with a low gas burner hiss and the faint creak of a steaming bamboo basket, the dry shuffle of a flour dusting, three soft doughy footfalls on metal tray, one short airy whoosh as he lunges, a clean heavy plop into broth, then a gentle simmer with one small bubble popping.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: A light pizzicato cello figure at a moderate tempo that follows the dumpling's footsteps, drops out completely during the lunge and the plop, and returns on a single dry resolved note as the cook straightens up.",
      "prefill": true,
      "help": "Describe the action, the camera and the sound. Put spoken words in quotes.",
      "bind": [
        {
          "node": "140:131",
          "field": "prompt"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "duration",
      "type": "slider",
      "label": "Duration (s)",
      "min": 1,
      "max": 20,
      "step": 0.5,
      "default": 5,
      "help": "Snapped to H3's 17k+5 frame grid at 24 fps (5 s → 124 frames).",
      "bind": [
        {
          "node": "140:133",
          "field": "value"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "aspect",
      "type": "select",
      "label": "Aspect ratio",
      "default": "16:9 (Widescreen)",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "1:1 (Square)",
          "label": "1:1"
        },
        {
          "value": "2:3 (Portrait Photo)",
          "label": "2:3"
        },
        {
          "value": "3:2 (Photo)",
          "label": "3:2"
        },
        {
          "value": "3:4 (Portrait Standard)",
          "label": "3:4"
        },
        {
          "value": "4:3 (Standard)",
          "label": "4:3"
        },
        {
          "value": "9:16 (Portrait Widescreen)",
          "label": "9:16"
        },
        {
          "value": "16:9 (Widescreen)",
          "label": "16:9"
        },
        {
          "value": "21:9 (Ultrawide)",
          "label": "21:9"
        }
      ],
      "bind": [
        {
          "node": "115",
          "field": "aspect_ratio"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "megapixels",
      "type": "slider",
      "label": "Resolution (MP)",
      "min": 0.2,
      "max": 1.5,
      "step": 0.02,
      "default": 0.98,
      "help": "0.98 MP ≈ 1344×768 at 16:9, rounded to a multiple of 32.",
      "bind": [
        {
          "node": "115",
          "field": "megapixels"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "unet_name",
      "type": "select",
      "label": "Diffusion model (DiT)",
      "default": "minimax_h3_fl2va_pruned_int8_convrot.safetensors",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "minimax_h3_fl2va_pruned_int8_convrot.safetensors",
          "label": "MiniMax H3 FL2VA int8 — default, matches this graph"
        },
        {
          "value": "minimax_h3_ref2va_pruned_int8_convrot.safetensors",
          "label": "MiniMax H3 Ref2VA int8 — reference-to-video, not this graph"
        },
        {
          "value": "minimax_h3_image_pruned_int8_convrot.safetensors",
          "label": "MiniMax H3 Image int8 — image generation, not this graph"
        }
      ],
      "help": "The diffusion transformer. FL2VA is the checkpoint this graph's conditioning expects; the Ref2VA and Image checkpoints are H3 siblings for other tasks and will not produce a valid clip here.",
      "bind": [
        {
          "node": "140:127",
          "field": "unet_name"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "vae_name",
      "type": "select",
      "label": "Video VAE",
      "default": "minimax_h3_video_vae_int8_convrot.safetensors",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "minimax_h3_video_vae_int8_convrot.safetensors",
          "label": "H3 video VAE int8 — default, 3.2 GB"
        },
        {
          "value": "minimax_h3_video_vae_fp16.safetensors",
          "label": "H3 video VAE fp16 — 5.2 GB, higher precision"
        },
        {
          "value": "minimax_h3_lynnreal_light_vae_int8_convrot.safetensors",
          "label": "H3 LynnReal Light VAE int8 — 2.1 GB, lighter/faster"
        }
      ],
      "help": "The video VAE that decodes the sampled latent. int8 is the default on this GPU; fp16 is heavier and higher precision; LynnReal Light is the smallest and fastest.",
      "bind": [
        {
          "node": "140:119",
          "field": "vae_name"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sampling",
      "type": "select",
      "label": "Sampling",
      "default": "pika",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "pika",
          "label": "Pika 6-step ladder (shipped)",
          "sets": [
            {
              "node": "140:125",
              "field": "sigmas",
              "value": [
                "140:143",
                0
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "value": "custom",
          "label": "Custom steps + sampler",
          "sets": [
            {
              "node": "140:125",
              "field": "sigmas",
              "value": [
                "140:160",
                0
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "help": "The Pika ladder is the shipped 6-step lcm schedule. Custom uses the Steps and Sampler below through a BasicScheduler; picking a turbo LoRA switches to Custom automatically."
    },
    {
      "id": "steps",
      "type": "slider",
      "label": "Steps",
      "min": 2,
      "max": 30,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 6,
      "help": "Only used with Custom sampling; the Pika ladder is fixed at 6 steps. Picking a LoRA above sets its trained step count.",
      "bind": [
        {
          "node": "140:160",
          "field": "steps"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sampler",
      "type": "select",
      "label": "Sampler",
      "default": "lcm",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "euler",
          "label": "euler"
        },
        {
          "value": "res_multistep",
          "label": "res_multistep"
        },
        {
          "value": "lcm",
          "label": "lcm"
        },
        {
          "value": "dpmpp_2m",
          "label": "dpmpp_2m"
        },
        {
          "value": "dpmpp_2m_sde",
          "label": "dpmpp_2m_sde"
        },
        {
          "value": "dpmpp_3m_sde",
          "label": "dpmpp_3m_sde"
        },
        {
          "value": "deis",
          "label": "deis"
        },
        {
          "value": "heun",
          "label": "heun"
        },
        {
          "value": "dpm_2",
          "label": "dpm_2"
        },
        {
          "value": "dpm_2_ancestral",
          "label": "dpm_2_ancestral"
        },
        {
          "value": "lms",
          "label": "lms"
        }
      ],
      "help": "lcm is what the Pika LoRA and its sigma ladder were built for. euler is what the TaoMate 3-step LoRA expects.",
      "bind": [
        {
          "node": "140:123",
          "field": "sampler_name"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lora_name",
      "type": "select",
      "label": "LoRA",
      "default": "pika_h3_flex_fl2va_v1_bf16.safetensors",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "pika_h3_flex_fl2va_v1_bf16.safetensors",
          "label": "Pika H3 Flex FL2VA v1 — default, 6-step ladder",
          "sync": {
            "steps": 6,
            "sampler": "lcm",
            "sampling": "pika"
          }
        },
        {
          "value": "taomate_h3_3step_comfy.safetensors",
          "label": "TaoMate H3 3-step — fastest, 3-step",
          "sync": {
            "steps": 3,
            "sampler": "euler",
            "sampling": "custom"
          }
        },
        {
          "value": "minimax_h3_fl2v_turbo_4step_v1.2_768p_comfyui_bf16.safetensors",
          "label": "MiniMax H3 FL2V turbo 4-step v1.2 768p",
          "sync": {
            "steps": 4,
            "sampler": "euler",
            "sampling": "custom"
          }
        },
        {
          "value": "minimax_h3_fl2v_turbo_8step_v1.0_comfyui_bf16.safetensors",
          "label": "MiniMax H3 FL2V turbo 8-step v1.0",
          "sync": {
            "steps": 8,
            "sampler": "euler",
            "sampling": "custom"
          }
        },
        {
          "value": "minimax_h3_DMAD_4step_full_lora_avg_rank_39_bf16.safetensors",
          "label": "MiniMax H3 DMAD 4-step",
          "sync": {
            "steps": 4,
            "sampler": "euler",
            "sampling": "custom"
          }
        },
        {
          "value": "minimax_h3_pdmd_2step_lora_avg_rank_38_bf16.safetensors",
          "label": "MiniMax H3 PDMD 2-step",
          "sync": {
            "steps": 2,
            "sampler": "euler",
            "sampling": "custom"
          }
        },
        {
          "value": "minimax_h3_pdmd_4step_lora_avg_rank_57_bf16.safetensors",
          "label": "MiniMax H3 PDMD 4-step",
          "sync": {
            "steps": 4,
            "sampler": "euler",
            "sampling": "custom"
          }
        },
        {
          "value": "minimax_h3_turbo_v4_step600_ema_comfyui.safetensors",
          "label": "MiniMax H3 turbo v4 step600 EMA (4-step)",
          "sync": {
            "steps": 4,
            "sampler": "euler",
            "sampling": "custom"
          }
        }
      ],
      "help": "The LoRA patched onto the diffusion model. Picking a turbo LoRA also sets its trained step count and sampler; the files live in ComfyUI/models/loras.",
      "bind": [
        {
          "node": "140:134",
          "field": "lora_name"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lora_strength",
      "type": "slider",
      "label": "LoRA strength",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 1.5,
      "step": 0.05,
      "default": 1,
      "help": "1.0 is the trained strength. Lower blends the base model back in; higher pushes the LoRA look harder.",
      "bind": [
        {
          "node": "140:134",
          "field": "strength_model"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "seed",
      "type": "seed",
      "label": "Seed",
      "default": 20261220,
      "help": "-1 picks a random seed.",
      "bind": [
        {
          "node": "140:129",
          "field": "noise_seed"
        },
        {
          "node": "vsr_sampler",
          "field": "seed"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clip_name",
      "type": "select",
      "label": "Text encoder",
      "default": "qwen3vl_32b_minimax_h3_int8_convrot.safetensors",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "qwen3vl_32b_minimax_h3_int8_convrot.safetensors",
          "label": "Qwen3-VL 32B int8 — native on gfx1151"
        },
        {
          "value": "qwen3vl_32b_minimax_h3_nvfp4_awq.safetensors",
          "label": "Qwen3-VL 32B nvfp4 — emulated, slower"
        },
        {
          "value": "qwen3vl_32b_minimax_h3_ultra_uncensored_heretic_int8_convrot.safetensors",
          "label": "Qwen3-VL 32B heretic int8"
        }
      ],
      "help": "int8 runs natively on gfx1151; nvfp4 is emulated here and encodes slower.",
      "bind": [
        {
          "node": "140:128",
          "field": "clip_name"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sla",
      "type": "toggle",
      "label": "Sparse attention (H3 SLA)",
      "default": true,
      "help": "ROCm sparse-attention patch. Turn it off (or run a backend without the node) and it is bypassed: the model goes straight to the guider.",
      "bind": [
        {
          "node": "sla",
          "field": "enabled"
        }
      ],
      "bypass": [
        {
          "node": "sla",
          "field": "model"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sla_detail",
      "type": "slider",
      "label": "SLA sparsity",
      "min": 0.8,
      "max": 0.95,
      "step": 0.05,
      "default": 0.85,
      "help": "Fraction of key blocks skipped. 0.85 is the shipped default the SLA turbo LoRA was distilled against; 0.90 is about 15% faster.",
      "bind": [
        {
          "node": "sla",
          "field": "sparsity_ratio"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sla_block_size",
      "type": "select",
      "label": "SLA block size",
      "default": "64",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "32",
          "label": "32 — finest, best for speech"
        },
        {
          "value": "64",
          "label": "64 — balanced (default)"
        },
        {
          "value": "128",
          "label": "128 — fastest, video only"
        }
      ],
      "help": "How many sequence tokens share one key selection. 64 is the ROCm node's default; 32 is finer and better for speech, 128 is faster but can make audio robotic.",
      "bind": [
        {
          "node": "sla",
          "field": "block_size"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sla_min_seq_len",
      "type": "number",
      "label": "SLA min sequence length",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 1000000,
      "step": 1024,
      "default": 8192,
      "help": "Sequences shorter than this stay dense. Lower it only when you know the clip is long enough to benefit.",
      "bind": [
        {
          "node": "sla",
          "field": "min_seq_len"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sla_dense_last_steps",
      "type": "slider",
      "label": "SLA dense last steps",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 8,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 0,
      "help": "Run the last N sampling steps at full attention. 0 matches the turbo LoRA's distillation setup; 1 can recover fine detail for a little more time.",
      "bind": [
        {
          "node": "sla",
          "field": "dense_last_steps"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sla_protect_audio",
      "type": "toggle",
      "label": "SLA protect audio",
      "default": true,
      "help": "Always attend audio and language-token blocks. Turn it off only for turbo-style uniform sparsity.",
      "bind": [
        {
          "node": "sla",
          "field": "protect_audio"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sla_stabilize_motion",
      "type": "toggle",
      "label": "SLA stabilize motion",
      "default": false,
      "help": "Bias block selection toward the previous step to reduce faint double-exposure on fast motion. Uses more VRAM.",
      "bind": [
        {
          "node": "sla",
          "field": "stabilize_motion"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sla_h3_cache",
      "type": "toggle",
      "label": "H3 cache",
      "default": false,
      "help": "Apply the H3 block-stack residual cache before SLA (fixed settings).",
      "bind": [
        {
          "node": "sla",
          "field": "h3_cache"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sla_reference_protection",
      "type": "toggle",
      "label": "SLA protect video refs",
      "default": false,
      "help": "Protect image/video reference blocks in Light mode. Only matters for reference-driven graphs.",
      "bind": [
        {
          "node": "sla",
          "field": "reference_protection"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sla_dense_steps",
      "type": "text",
      "label": "SLA dense steps",
      "default": "",
      "help": "Explicit 0-based step indices to force dense, for example '0,1' or '0-2'. Blank means none.",
      "bind": [
        {
          "node": "sla",
          "field": "dense_steps"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sla_dense_backend",
      "type": "select",
      "label": "SLA dense backend",
      "default": "comfy_kitchen",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "comfy_kitchen",
          "label": "comfy_kitchen (default)"
        },
        {
          "value": "pytorch",
          "label": "pytorch (reference, no quantization)"
        },
        {
          "value": "auto",
          "label": "auto (whatever is active)"
        },
        {
          "value": "sage:auto",
          "label": "sage:auto"
        },
        {
          "value": "sage:qk_int8_pv_fp16_cuda",
          "label": "sage:qk_int8_pv_fp16_cuda"
        },
        {
          "value": "sage:qk_int8_pv_fp16_triton",
          "label": "sage:qk_int8_pv_fp16_triton"
        },
        {
          "value": "sage:qk_int8_pv_fp8_cuda",
          "label": "sage:qk_int8_pv_fp8_cuda"
        },
        {
          "value": "sage:qk_int8_pv_fp8_cuda++",
          "label": "sage:qk_int8_pv_fp8_cuda++"
        }
      ],
      "help": "Kernel used on dense fall-through steps. comfy_kitchen is the fast default; pytorch is the exact reference.",
      "bind": [
        {
          "node": "sla",
          "field": "dense_backend"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sla_disable_fp16_accum",
      "type": "toggle",
      "label": "SLA disable fp16 accumulation",
      "default": true,
      "help": "Force off the reduced-precision matmul reduction path. Recommended on H3.",
      "bind": [
        {
          "node": "sla",
          "field": "disable_fp16_accum"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "upscale",
      "type": "select",
      "label": "Upscale",
      "default": "",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "",
          "label": "None — native model resolution"
        },
        {
          "value": "x2",
          "label": "2× — RelayVSR x2 (lightx2v DIT + Flash VAE)",
          "sets": [
            {
              "node": "vsr_unet",
              "field": "unet_name",
              "value": "relayvsr_x2_lightx2v_int8_convrot.safetensors"
            },
            {
              "node": "vsr_vae",
              "field": "vae_name",
              "value": "relayvsr_flash_vae_x2_fp32.safetensors"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "value": "x4",
          "label": "4× — RelayVSR x4 (the paper's 4× model)",
          "sets": [
            {
              "node": "vsr_unet",
              "field": "unet_name",
              "value": "relayvsr_x4_int8_convrot.safetensors"
            },
            {
              "node": "vsr_vae",
              "field": "vae_name",
              "value": "relayvsr_flash_vae_x4_fp32.safetensors"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "help": "Optional RelayVSR pass on the decoded frames before encoding: the DIT decides the factor and the Flash VAE of the same factor restores the frames it skips. None keeps the native result; x4 multiplies pixels by 16 and is slow.",
      "bypass": [
        {
          "node": "vsr_decode",
          "field": "images"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "upscale_detail",
      "type": "slider",
      "label": "Upscale detail",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 1,
      "step": 0.05,
      "default": 1,
      "help": "RelayVSR: how much of what the Flash decoder adds on top of a plain bicubic upscale is kept. 1 is the full model output, lower is calmer and closer to the source.",
      "bind": [
        {
          "node": "vsr_decode",
          "field": "detail"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "filename_prefix",
      "type": "text",
      "label": "File name prefix",
      "default": "riverfield/pika-text-to-video",
      "bind": [
        {
          "node": "92",
          "field": "filename_prefix"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "format",
      "type": "select",
      "label": "Container",
      "default": "mp4",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "mp4",
          "label": "mp4"
        },
        {
          "value": "mkv",
          "label": "mkv"
        },
        {
          "value": "webm",
          "label": "webm"
        },
        {
          "value": "mov",
          "label": "mov"
        },
        {
          "value": "auto",
          "label": "auto"
        }
      ],
      "bind": [
        {
          "node": "92",
          "field": "format"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "codec",
